# Environment Configuration for Chainlink Integration

This file documents all environment variables needed for Chainlink oracle integration with goal.live.

## Copy this template to your `.env.local` file and fill in actual values

```bash
# ============================================
# CHAINLINK ORACLE CONFIGURATION
# ============================================

# Chainlink Functions Router Address (chain-specific)
# Solana: Use SPL-wrapped Chainlink address
VITE_CHAINLINK_ROUTER_ADDRESS=0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000000

# Decentralized Oracle Network ID
# For Solana Devnet: fun-solana-devnet-1
# For Solana Testnet: fun-solana-testnet-1
VITE_CHAINLINK_DON_ID=fun-solana-devnet-1

# Chainlink Subscription ID (obtained from Chainlink dashboard)
VITE_CHAINLINK_SUBSCRIPTION_ID=1

# Gas limit for oracle callback (in units of gas)
# Typical range: 100000-300000
VITE_CHAINLINK_GAS_LIMIT=200000

# Callback function name in your smart contract
VITE_CHAINLINK_CALLBACK_FUNCTION=fulfillOddsRequest

# ============================================
# SPORTS DATA CONFIGURATION
# ============================================

# Environment mode: development, testnet, mainnet
VITE_ENVIRONMENT=development

# Whether to use real Chainlink oracle (false for development/mock)
VITE_USE_CHAINLINK_ORACLE=false

# Preferred blockchain: solana or ethereum
VITE_CHAIN=solana

# ============================================
# SOLANA CONFIGURATION
# ============================================

# Solana RPC endpoint
VITE_SOLANA_RPC_URL=https://api.devnet.solana.com

# Solana cluster: devnet, testnet, mainnet-beta
VITE_SOLANA_CLUSTER=devnet

# Your Solana program ID (deploy and set this)
VITE_SOLANA_PROGRAM_ID=11111111111111111111111111111111

# ============================================
# BETTING BOT CONFIGURATION (Optional)
# ============================================

# Enable automated betting bot
VITE_BOT_ENABLED=false

# Maximum bet size in USDC
VITE_BOT_MAX_BET_SIZE=5

# Minimum odds threshold for placing bets
VITE_BOT_MIN_ODDS=1.5

# Maximum odds threshold for placing bets
VITE_BOT_MAX_ODDS=10

# Refresh interval in milliseconds
VITE_BOT_REFRESH_INTERVAL=10000

# ============================================
# API KEYS & SECRETS
# ============================================

# Sports data API key (if using external API in future)
VITE_SPORTS_API_KEY=

# Chainlink coordinator private key (for testnet only!)
# NEVER commit this to git
VITE_CHAINLINK_PRIVATE_KEY=

# ============================================
# DEVELOPMENT ONLY
# ============================================

# Enable debug logging
VITE_DEBUG=false

# Mock only mode (skip oracle calls)
VITE_MOCK_ONLY=true

# Simulate oracle latency (milliseconds)
VITE_ORACLE_LATENCY_MS=0
```

## Environment-Specific Setups

### Development (Local Testing with Mock Data)

```bash
VITE_ENVIRONMENT=development
VITE_USE_CHAINLINK_ORACLE=false
VITE_CHAIN=solana
VITE_SOLANA_CLUSTER=devnet
VITE_MOCK_ONLY=true
VITE_DEBUG=true
```

### Devnet Testnet (Real Chainlink Functions)

```bash
VITE_ENVIRONMENT=testnet
VITE_USE_CHAINLINK_ORACLE=true
VITE_CHAIN=solana
VITE_SOLANA_CLUSTER=devnet
VITE_CHAINLINK_DON_ID=fun-solana-devnet-1
# Get subscription ID from https://functions.chain.link/solana/devnet
VITE_CHAINLINK_SUBSCRIPTION_ID=
```

### Production (Solana Mainnet)

```bash
VITE_ENVIRONMENT=mainnet
VITE_USE_CHAINLINK_ORACLE=true
VITE_CHAIN=solana
VITE_SOLANA_CLUSTER=mainnet-beta
VITE_CHAINLINK_DON_ID=fun-solana-mainnet-1
# Obtain from Chainlink
VITE_CHAINLINK_SUBSCRIPTION_ID=
```

## Getting Chainlink Credentials

### 1. Chainlink Functions Subscription

1. Go to [Chainlink Functions Dashboard](https://functions.chain.link/solana/devnet)
2. Connect your wallet
3. Create a new subscription
4. Save the subscription ID to `VITE_CHAINLINK_SUBSCRIPTION_ID`

### 2. Solana Program ID

After deploying your Solana program:

```bash
# Deploy your program
solana program deploy path/to/program.so

# Program ID will be printed to console
# Add to VITE_SOLANA_PROGRAM_ID
```

### 3. Chainlink DON ID

Available DON IDs:

| Network | DON ID |
| ------- | ------ |
| Solana Devnet | `fun-solana-devnet-1` |
| Solana Testnet | `fun-solana-testnet-1` |
| Solana Mainnet | `fun-solana-mainnet-1` |

## Validation

After setting up `.env.local`, verify your configuration:

```bash
# Test Chainlink connection
npm run test:chainlink

# Verify all env vars are loaded
console.log(import.meta.env.VITE_CHAINLINK_SUBSCRIPTION_ID)

# Dry-run oracle request
npm run test:oracle
```

## Security Best Practices

⚠️ **NEVER commit `.env.local` to git**

- Add `.env.local` to `.gitignore` ✅
- Keep private keys in secure key management (e.g., AWS Secrets Manager)
- Use different keys for dev/testnet/mainnet
- Rotate keys regularly
- Enable key rotation on Chainlink subscription

## Troubleshooting

### "DON ID not found"

- Verify DON ID matches your network (devnet/testnet/mainnet)
- Check Chainlink Functions dashboard for available DON IDs

### "Subscription not found"

- Create subscription at https://functions.chain.link
- Ensure subscription ID is correct
- Verify wallet is connected to correct network

### "Program ID invalid"

- Redeploy your Solana program
- Update `VITE_SOLANA_PROGRAM_ID` with new program ID
- Verify program exists on-chain: `solana account <PROGRAM_ID>`

### "Oracle callback gas limit exceeded"

- Increase `VITE_CHAINLINK_GAS_LIMIT`
- Optimize callback function in smart contract
- Split into multiple callbacks if needed

